# the startup splash at 40x120 (TUI-DESIGN-2 §5, H-A1w; TUI-DESIGN-3 §3 F-W1w): the same scenario as splash.steps in the wide geometry —
# the key completes the reveal, the resting mark (with the tagline `Decisions, not strings` at ≥ 104 columns) stays under the rule; 0 clears
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect step 0/
# raw mode on (Ink's post-commit effect writes ESC[?2004h): a key sent earlier is a cooked-mode byte the kernel echoes
expect \x1b\[\?2004h
sleep 0.1
send h
expect (?:›|>) (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*h
sleep 0.3
send \x03
expect Say hi
expect sess \$
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
